By default, Material-UI (MUI) tries to be "smart"—if it thinks there isn't enough space at the bottom of your screen, it will automatically flip the dropdowns to open upwards.
To override this and **force them to strictly open downwards**, we need to turn off the "flip" modifier in the Autocompletes, and firmly anchor the Select fields to the bottom.
Here are the precise updates for your Data Entry Grid in **JournalPosting.js**:
### 1. Fix Branch & CGL (The Autocompletes)
For <Autocomplete>, MUI uses a Popper engine. We can pass slotProps to disable the flip behavior.
Find your **Branch** <Autocomplete> (around line 524) and **CGL** <Autocomplete> (around line 560), and add this exact property to both of them:
```javascript
  slotProps={{
    popper: {
      placement: 'bottom-start',
      modifiers: [
        {
          name: 'flip',
          enabled: false, // Forces it to never flip upwards
        },
        {
          name: 'preventOverflow',
          enabled: false, // Prevents it from jumping around
        }
      ],
    },
  }}

```
**Example of where to put it (Branch):**
```javascript
<Autocomplete
  popupIcon={null} 
  autoHighlight 
  options={branchSearch.options}
  getOptionLabel={(option) => option && option.code ? `${option.code} - ${option.name}` : ""}
  value={row.branch || null}
  onChange={(event, newValue) => handleRowChange(row.id, "branch", newValue)}
  
  // --- ADD THIS BLOCK HERE ---
  slotProps={{
    popper: {
      placement: 'bottom-start',
      modifiers: [{ name: 'flip', enabled: false }, { name: 'preventOverflow', enabled: false }],
    },
  }}
  // ---------------------------
  
  inputValue={branchInputValues[row.id] || ""}
  // ... rest of the code

```
### 2. Fix Txn Type (The Select Dropdown)
Your Txn Type field is a <TextField select>. To force it down, we must add MenuProps to anchor it to the bottom of the input box.
Find the **Txn Type** <TextField select> (around line 603) and replace its SelectProps with this:
```javascript
  SelectProps={{ 
    displayEmpty: true, 
    renderValue: (selected) => !selected ? <span style={{ color: 'gray', opacity: 0.8 }}>Type</span> : selected,
    
    // --- ADDED THIS TO FORCE DOWNWARDS ---
    MenuProps: { 
      anchorOrigin: { vertical: "bottom", horizontal: "left" }, 
      transformOrigin: { vertical: "top", horizontal: "left" }, 
      PaperProps: { style: { maxHeight: 200 } },
      marginThreshold: 0 // Prevents MUI from pushing it up if it nears the screen edge
    } 
  }}

```
### 3. Update Currency (The Select Dropdown)
You already have MenuProps on your Currency field, but we should add marginThreshold: 0 to guarantee it doesn't bounce up when the user scrolls near the bottom of the page.
Find the **Currency** <TextField select> (around line 550) and update its SelectProps to match this:
```javascript
  SelectProps={{ 
    displayEmpty: true, 
    renderValue: (selected) => !selected ? <span style={{ color: 'gray', opacity: 0.8 }}>Select Currency</span> : selected, 
    MenuProps: { 
      anchorOrigin: { vertical: "bottom", horizontal: "left" }, 
      transformOrigin: { vertical: "top", horizontal: "left" }, 
      PaperProps: { style: { maxHeight: 250 } },
      marginThreshold: 0 // <-- ADD THIS
    } 
  }}

```
With these 3 small changes applied, every single dropdown in your grid will now rigidly drop downwards, giving you a much cleaner and more predictable user experience!
